gins":0.1337,"operating_margins":0.06846,"profit_margins":0.03019,"net_income":19216000.0,"total_cash":2450000.0,"total_cash_per_share":0.345,"total_debt":100906000.0,"debt_to_equity":66.607,"current_ratio":3.375,"free_cashflow":-42873624.0,"return_on_equity":0.1376,"enterprise_value":337409856.0,"enterprise_to_ebitda":10.964,"enterprise_to_revenue":0.522,"earnings_growth":0.701,"shares_outstanding":7107491.0,"float_shares":6605134.0,"held_pct_insiders":0.07068,"held_pct_institutions":0.53748,"beta":1.564,"fifty_two_week_high":37.97,"fifty_two_week_low":14.51,"fifty_day_average":25.54,"two_hundred_day_avg":21.2233,"recommendation":"none","all_time_high":37.97,"all_time_low":1.289218,"long_business_summary":"Friedman Industries, Incorporated engages in the manufacture and processing of steel products in the United States. The company operates in two segments, Flat-Roll Products and Tubular Products. The Flat-Roll Product segment is involved in the operation of hot-rolled coil processing facilities to cut the coils into sheets and plates, as well as the provision of process and storage services for customer-owned coils on a fee basis. The Tubular Product segment manufactures line and oil country pipes, as well as pipes for structural applications. The company serves metals distributors and customers manufacturing products, such as metal buildings, railcars, heavy equipment, tanks and containers, trailers, component parts, and other fabricated metal products. Friedman Industries, Incorporated was incorporated in 1965 and is headquartered in Longview, Texas."}}